   "author": "4b5a977bb2913635",
   "date": "2016-09-27T06:52:42Z",
   "subject": "Description of the \"self object\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\">In the source code of ggplot, it is often refered to a &quot;<font face=\"courier new, monospace\">self </font>object&quot; and different slots therein. For example, in <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/blob/master/R/scale-.r\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/blob/master/R/scale-.r&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367674615000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0wA3umH5uy_Z_UiUyxWWWG\">scale-.r</a> we find, among others, <font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">self</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">get_limits(), </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">self</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">breaks, </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">self</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">break_positions()</span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;white-space:pre\">. </span></font><span style=\"font-size:small\">&quot;</span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"font-size:small\">self&quot; </font><font style=\"font-size:small\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">is mentioned in </font><span style=\"font-size:small\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace;font-size:small;white-space:pre\">?ggroto, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:small;white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">but I fail to find information about the slots the way they are used in the ggplot code.</font></span><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Can someone please point me to relevant documentation of </font></span></font><span style=\"font-size:small\">&quot;</span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"font-size:small\">self</font><span style=\"font-size:small\">&quot; and its different slots.  </span><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> </font></span></font></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "4CHbHwl7BAAJ",
   "from": "Brian",
   "author": "f20966e9bc9cf5c7",
   "date": "2016-09-27T09:25:34Z",
   "subject": "Re: Description of the \"self object\"",
   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "<div>Hi Henrik,<br>\r\nAs you probably know you are looking at reference class R code:<br>\r\n<br>\r\n<a href=\"http://adv-r.had.co.nz/R5.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://adv-r.had.co.nz/R5.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367674617000&amp;usg=AOvVaw0Yq1gNmUdQyWrX5Ga4bu6X\">http://adv-r.had.co.nz/R5.html</a><br>\r\n<br>\r\nI remember Hadley mentioning a new object orientation class used for the last (2.0?) ggplot2 release. If true and undocumented, I guess the &quot;self&quot; refers to containing object (Class) - as it does in python. Otherwise this is inherent to the reference class.<br>\r\n<br>\r\nHTH,<br>\r\nBrian</div>"
    ],
    [
     3,
     "<div><br>\r\n<br><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\">El 27 de septiembre de 2016 8:52:41 AM GMT+02:00, Henrik &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">henri...@gmail.com</a>&gt; escribió:<blockquote class=\"gmail_quote\" style=\"margin:0pt 0pt 0pt 0.8ex;border-left:1px solid rgb(204,204,204);padding-left:1ex\">\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\"><font size=\"2\">In the source code of ggplot, it is often refered to a &quot;<font face=\"courier new, monospace\">self </font>object&quot; and different slots therein. For example, in <a href=\"https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/blob/master/R/scale-.r\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=https://github.com/hadley/ggplot2/blob/master/R/scale-.r&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367674617000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1sJaHprzjRumLxUjnDFBmS\">scale-.r</a> we find, among others, <font face=\"courier new, monospace\"><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">self</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">get_limits(), </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">self</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">breaks, </span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">self</span><span style=\"box-sizing:border-box;color:rgb(167,29,93);white-space:pre\">$</span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\">break_positions()</span></font><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:Consolas,&quot;Liberation Mono&quot;,Menlo,Courier,monospace;white-space:pre\">. </span></font><span style=\"font-size:small\">&quot;</span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"font-size:small\">self&quot; </font><font style=\"font-size:small\" face=\"arial, sans-serif\">is mentioned in </font><span style=\"font-size:small\"> </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-family:&quot;courier new&quot;,monospace;font-size:small;white-space:pre\">?ggroto, </span><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);font-size:small;white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">but I fail to find information about the slots the way they are used in the ggplot code.</font></span><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"><br></font></span></font></div><div><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\">Can someone please point me to relevant documentation of </font></span></font><span style=\"font-size:small\">&quot;</span><font face=\"courier new, monospace\" style=\"font-size:small\">self</font><span style=\"font-size:small\">&quot; and its different slots.  </span><font size=\"2\"><span style=\"color:rgb(51,51,51);white-space:pre\"><font face=\"arial, sans-serif\"> </font></span></font></div></div>\r\n\r\n<p></p>\r\n</blockquote></div></div>"
    ]
   ]
  },
  {
   "id": "ZcYsv4QYBQAJ",
