     "<p dir=\"ltr\">There is some documentation at <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367674622000&amp;usg=AOvVaw1XlTF3xEMj6xvAl9lzha0j\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.html</a>, but presumably self is used to refer to an object from inside one of its methods.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Best,<br>\r\nIsta</p>\r\n<div class=\"gmail_extra\"><br><div class=\"gmail_quote\"></div></div>"
    ],
    [
