   "parts": [
    [
     1,
     "Hi Henrik,\r<br>\r<br>who knows where you are at in programming knowledge and what you exactly \r<br>want to do. I have a feeling that Ista&#39;s tip is the right one - you want \r<br>to extend ggplot2. If you are familiar with OO-languages, e.g. python, \r<br>then R5 is a breeze.  Otherwise, it can be intimidating at first. I \r<br>suggest starting with some documentation. Then digging/tunneling won&#39;t \r<br>be confusing.\r<br>\r<br>Slots belong to S4. In R5, &quot;fields are the equivalent of slots in S4.&quot;\r<br>\r<br>Good luck,\r<br>Brian\r<br>"
    ],
    [
     2,
     "\r<br>\r<br>On 09/29/2016 01:20 PM, Ista Zahn wrote:\r<br>&gt; There is some documentation at\r<br>&gt; <a href=\"http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.html\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"nofollow\" data-saferedirecturl=\"https://www.google.com/url?hl=en-US&amp;q=http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.html&amp;source=gmail&amp;ust=1792367674624000&amp;usg=AOvVaw17qAh_oqdFsdgWO9E4Dwa1\">http://docs.ggplot2.org/current/vignettes/extending-ggplot2.html</a>, but\r<br>&gt; presumably self is used to refer to an object from inside one of its\r<br>&gt; methods.\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; Best,\r<br>&gt; Ista\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt;\r<br>&gt; On Sep 29, 2016 5:31 AM, &quot;Henrik&quot; &lt;<a href data-email-masked rel=\"nofollow\">henri...@gmail.com</a>\r<br>"
    ],
